# text = When I look upon the tombs of the great , every motion of envy dies in me ; when I read the epitaphs of the beautiful , every inordinate desire goes out ; when I meet with the grief of parents upon a tombstone , my heart melts with compassion ; when I see the tombs of the parents themselves , I consider the vanity of grieving for those whom we must quickly follow By Jove -- I had quite forgotten my sweet-faced cousin , and that she's here all the time ! ... and my old schoolmaster , too sentiment For wisdom is a defence , and money is a defence ; but the excellency of knowledge is , that wisdom giveth life to them that have it A sweet , saintly , Christian business , hers Spaik when he heave !
